      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The sum of each row is the sum of the elements of a polygon.\n\nLet $i$ be odd $1\\leq i\\leq 100$.\n\nThen\n\\begin{align}\ni + i + (i+2) &= 3i+2 \\\\\n(i+1)^2 + (i+3)^2 &= 2i^2 + 8i + 10 \\\\\n(i+2)^3 + (i+1)^3 &= 3i^3 +16i^2 + 57i + 15\n\\end{align}\nCall a number $a_j$ to be acceptable in Row $j$ if ${3a_j \\over 2}$ is an integer in Row $j+1$ and ${4a_j \\over 3}$ is an integer in Row $j-1$.\n\nFor example, in Row 1, 3 odd numbers are acceptable: $\\{1,5,9\\}$.\n\nFor Row $j-1$, three odd numbers must be acceptable: ${9 \\over 2}$ must be an odd integer. This forces $j=3$. So Row 2 must have three acceptable numbers: 1, 9, 25.\n\nFor Row $j-1$, three more odd numbers must be acceptable: ${16 \\over 3}$ must be an odd integer. This forces $j=4$. So Row 3 must have four acceptable  numbers: $$17,33,169$$\n\nNow, for Row $j-1$, there are precisely two entries acceptable: ${15 \\over 2},57 \\over 3}$ forcing $j=5$. Thus, we have 8 acceptable entries in Row 4.\n\nIn rows 5, 6 and 7 we see that 2,3,4 entries are acceptable so that the 7th row has $\\boxed{9}$ acceptable numbers.\n\nThus, there are $\\boxed{185}$ entries in the array that are multiples of $67$. The answer is 185",
